From: termux-glibc-mesa <termux-glibc-mesa@local>
Subject: [PATCH] egl,glx: use Kopper (Vulkan) by default on Android/KGSL

On Adreno devices exposed through KGSL (Android's out-of-tree DRM driver)
there is no upstream freedreno *gallium* KMD: the only supported render
path is Turnip (Vulkan, tu_knl_kgsl.cc) reached through zink via Kopper.
Upstream only falls back to zink *after* the in-tree driver has failed to
initialize, which on a KGSL-only system is fatal rather than merely slow:

  * EGL (platform_x11.c): dri3_x11_connect() calls x11_dri3_open(), which
    needs a DRI3 render node fd.  KGSL has no /dev/dri/renderD*, and
    termux-x11 does not implement the DRI3 Open request either, so the
    probe fails and dri2_dpy->driver_name stays NULL.  If the X server
    also lacks DRI3 1.2 BuffersFromPixmap (x11_dri3_has_multibuffer()
    returns false), dri2_initialize_x11() returns EGL_FALSE outright and
    EGL silently degrades to swrast:

        EGL driver name: swrast
        MESA-EGL: warning: DRI3 error: Could not get DRI3 device

  * GLX (glxext.c): the missing-multibuffer check goes straight to
    init_fail with "DRI3 not available" whenever Zink was elected.

Kopper does not need any of that.  Its presentation path is
vkQueuePresentKHR() on a VkSwapchainKHR created from the XCB surface,
which lands in the Vulkan WSI DRI3 code and is exactly what the KGSL
WSI patch supports.  So:

  * EGL: default disp->Options.Zink to TRUE when
    MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE is unset (or "zink") and GALLIUM_DRIVER
    is unset, and treat Zink as forced when Kopper is available so the
    DRI3 probe is skipped instead of aborting initialisation.
  * GLX: pre-elect GLX_DRIVER_ZINK_YES in the same situation, and keep
    the "DRI3 not available" failure only for non-Kopper drivers.

Users can still opt out with MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE,
GALLIUM_DRIVER or LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE.
---
--- a/src/egl/main/eglapi.c
+++ b/src/egl/main/eglapi.c
@@ -684,7 +684,14 @@
                  "Found 'LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE' set, will use a CPU renderer");
 
       const char *env = os_get_option("MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE");
-      disp->Options.Zink = env && !strcmp(env, "zink");
+      /* Prefer zink unless the user explicitly asked for something else.
+       * On Android/KGSL this is the only hardware path (Turnip via
+       * Kopper): there is no DRM render node, so the DRI3 probe fails
+       * and upstream would only reach zink after a wasted round of
+       * screen setup, or never.
+       */
+      disp->Options.Zink = (!env || !strcmp(env, "zink")) &&
+                           !os_get_option("GALLIUM_DRIVER");
 
       const char *gallium_hud_env = os_get_option("GALLIUM_HUD");
       disp->Options.GalliumHudWarn =
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_x11.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_x11.c
@@ -1234,8 +1234,16 @@
    /* True if we're going to force-enable a HW Zink driver, even if the X
     * server is missing a bunch of features.
     */
+   /* On Android/KGSL there is no DRM render node, so the X11 DRI3 probe
+    * (dri3_x11_connect) always fails, and because termux-x11 does not
+    * implement the DRI3 Open request, driver_name cannot be resolved
+    * either.  Upstream then returns EGL_FALSE here and EGL silently
+    * falls back to swrast.  Treat Zink as forced whenever Kopper is
+    * available: that selects the pure-Vulkan (Turnip/KGSL)
+    * presentation path which does not need dri3_open at all.
+    */
    const bool force_zink =
-      disp->Options.Zink && debug_get_bool_option("LIBGL_KOPPER_DRI2", false);
+      disp->Options.Zink && !debug_get_bool_option("LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE", false);
 
    /*
     * Every hardware driver_name is set using strdup. Doing the same in
--- a/src/glx/glxext.c
+++ b/src/glx/glxext.c
@@ -989,7 +989,12 @@
    Bool kopper = !debug_get_bool_option("LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE", false);
 #endif
 
-   if (env && !strcmp(env, "zink"))
+   /* Prefer zink unless the user explicitly asked for something else.
+    * On Android/KGSL the in-tree freedreno gallium KMD is absent and
+    * loader_get_driver_for_fd() cannot name a driver for a KGSL fd, so
+    * electing zink up-front is the only way Kopper gets used.
+    */
+   if (!env || !strcmp(env, "zink"))
       glx_driver |= GLX_DRIVER_ZINK_YES;
 
    dpyPriv->drawHash = __glxHashCreate();
@@ -1025,7 +1030,15 @@
       glx_driver |= GLX_DRIVER_SW;
 
 #if !defined(GLX_USE_APPLEGL)
-   if (!dpyPriv->has_multibuffer && glx_accel && !debug_get_bool_option("LIBGL_KOPPER_DRI2", false)) {
+   /* termux-x11 does not implement DRI3 1.2 BuffersFromPixmap, so
+    * has_multibuffer is always false there.  That must not be fatal for
+    * Kopper/Zink: presentation goes through Vulkan
+    * (VkSwapchainKHR on the XCB surface), not through DRI3
+    * pixmap_from_buffer, so the multibuffer requirement does not apply.
+    * Keep the upstream check only for non-Kopper drivers.
+    */
+   if (!dpyPriv->has_multibuffer && glx_accel && !kopper &&
+       !debug_get_bool_option("LIBGL_KOPPER_DRI2", false)) {
       if (glx_driver & GLX_DRIVER_ZINK_YES) {
          /* only print error if zink was explicitly requested */
          CriticalErrorMessageF("DRI3 not available\n");
